From: Ritik B. <bompilwar.r@northeastern.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] fellows/ritik-b: register the "BLIP: Noisier Data, Better Model?" compositions

Registers 14 compositions in runtime/remotion/src/Root.tsx — seven responsive scene
components, each at 1920x1080 and 1080x1920, so the reel renders in both orientations
from one component set. `calculateMetadata` turns each scene's `durationS` prop into
`durationInFrames`, so a beat animates across its measured narration instead of
finishing early and freeze-holding the tail.

APPLY ORDER: this hunk's context sits directly below the registrations added by
fellows/ritik-b/2026-09-06-vqa-blind/patches/brutalist-toolkit.patch. Apply that patch
FIRST, then this one.

The eight scene files themselves are not patched — they do not exist in a clean clone.
Copy them from this reel's remotion/scenes/ into runtime/remotion/src/scenes/.

  ReelKit.tsx            the orientation-aware stage (promoted from VqaKit.tsx)
  ReelExecSummary.tsx    the Beat 2 BLUF        (promoted from VqaExecSummary.tsx)
  ReelFramework.tsx      the framework beat     (promoted from VqaFourMoves.tsx)
  BlipMed.tsx            one transformer, three functionalities
  BlipCapFilt.tsx        the worked example
  BlipIndependence.tsx   Table 4 — the confirmation-bias receipt
  BlipDiversity.tsx      Table 2 — the butterfly
  BlipLadder.tsx         Table 1 — the ablation on a declared truncated axis

Nothing else in the toolkit is modified by this reel.
